# Declare binary formats explicitly.
#
# Git already detects these by content, and on this machine Git for Windows'
# global gitattributes adds `*.pdf diff=astextplain` on top. But both of those
# are local: a fresh clone elsewhere, and GitHub's own file viewer, see only
# what the repository declares. Stating it here makes the classification travel
# with the repository instead of depending on whose machine it is on.
#
# `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff -merge`: never convert line endings,
# never attempt a textual diff, never try to merge hunks.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.zip   binary
*.jar   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
